{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01SUqP574SqDysBVk68XyKoR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CV2iNKcgX3casd5m4ujFxs","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np = \"TODO.md\"\ns = open(p).read()\ns = s.replace(\"- [ ] **sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone**\", \"- [x] **sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone**\")\nopen(p, \"w\").write(s)\np = \"KEY_DECISIONS.md\"\ns = open(p).read()\ns += \"\"\"- **sos_120:** Paradigm recast modeled as recasting the exiled card itself via `cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)` rather than `copy_spell` (TODO mentioned copy_spell, but copy_spell needs a stack object and its copies are not \"cast\" — Paradigm says \"you may CAST a copy\"). A permanent `SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent` redirect (stack→exile) implements both \"Then exile this spell\" and the return to exile after every recast; observably identical to casting a copy and avoids phantom copies in the graveyard. Paradigm registration is guarded by a once-flag so recasts don't double-register.\n\"\"\"\nopen(p, \"w\").write(s)\nEOF\ngit add -A && git commit -q -m \"sos_120: Improvisation Capstone\" && git log --oneline -1","description":"Mark TODO, log decision, commit sos_120"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1032,"cache_read_input_tokens":251518,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1032},"output_tokens":65,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"91030fde-ab39-43e5-99c8-7491eecaa6bd","uuid":"ec898d5a-d9e7-43bc-b3fe-293eb881c7a3","request_id":"req_011CbuwcgP3uz3SGp2ZuGugs"}
