{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01WkXP9BsrKaPxZNibMtqAwo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YKGP73kAytZshrHVGUqboj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np = \"TODO.md\"\ns = open(p).read()\ns = s.replace(\"- [ ] **sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares**\", \"- [x] **sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares**\")\nopen(p, \"w\").write(s)\np = \"KEY_DECISIONS.md\"\ns = open(p).read()\ns += \"\"\"- **sos_13:** Rulebook 722.3c confirmed: the Swords copy is created in exile when the permanent becomes prepared (not at cast time, as TODO suggested) and is cast for its normal {W} cost (no free-cast clause) — `cast_prepared_spell(game)` pays {W} then uses `cast_spell_free` for the stack plumbing. Casting the copy directly via `cast_spell_free` also works (unprepare happens in the copy's `on_cast`). A resolved copy ceases to exist via a `prevented` SpellToGraveyard replacement instead of hitting the graveyard.\n- **sos_13:** Engine fires the ETB event before registering the entering card's own triggers, so own-entry ETB effects must live in `on_resolve` (fdn_205 convention) — moved the token/prepared logic there; the creature counts itself as controlled since it enters as the spell resolves. \"Target player\" is chosen by the controller at resolution (trigger targeting is not modeled in this engine).\n\"\"\"\nopen(p, \"w\").write(s)\nEOF\ngit add -A && git commit -q -m \"sos_13: Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\" && git log --oneline -1","description":"Mark TODO, log decisions, commit sos_13"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1112,"cache_read_input_tokens":279630,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1112},"output_tokens":65,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"c