{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_014orsZMrncUygNSAdVQsR7R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All ten SOS cards are implemented and committed. The full workspace suite passes: **1258 tests green** (1145 engine regression tests — zero regressions — plus FDN reference tests and 64 new SOS tests), all ten card classes import and construct bare, every TODO item is checked off, and the tree is clean with one commit per item.\n\n**Shared engine changes (built first, all additive):**\n- **E1** — `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` now fires from `cast_spell` *and* `cast_spell_free` (a free cast is still a cast per rule 601; `copy_spell` copies correctly don't fire it).\n- **E2** — new `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent`, fired from `GameState.advance_phase` after `empty_mana_pools()` so handler-added mana survives into the main phase.\n- **E3** — `get_cost_reduction` now aggregates `spell_cost_reduction` from the caster's battlefield permanents for instant/sorcery casts.\n\n**The ten cards**, each with focused real-engine tests plus an independent throwaway smoke check: sos_4 (Converge via `colors_spent`), sos_1 (graveyard cost reduction, attack-trigger free cast, exile-instead), sos_245 (affinity self + grant via E3), sos_226 (Casualty 1 with spell copy), sos_257 (land with restricted mana + 2/4 Wizard animation + pump), sos_57 (counterspell + delayed {C}), sos_120 (exile-until-MV-4 + recurring Paradigm recast), sos_13 (Inkling token, prepared state, real Swords copy in exile per rule 722.3c), sos_201 (miracle {2} + opponent-upkeep loot), sos_97 (planeswalker: surveil/discard/reanimate/coin-flip skip-turns).\n\n**Where the plan and the engine disagreed**, I followed spec/rulebook and logged it in `KEY_DECISIONS.md` (12 entries). The notable ones: `AttacksTriggeredEvent` was defined but never fired — now fired in `declare_attackers_step`; spells moving stack→graveyard never consulted replacements — added `Spell